9.text:
The five exemplars are all 3-letter CVC items

* dad  = C a C
* dab  = C a C
* gut  = C u C
* low  = C o C
* cat  = C a C

with the middle vowel belonging to the set {a,u,o} and the final
consonant belonging to the set {b,d,t,w}.  That is

second ∈ {a,u,o}  ∧  third ∈ {b,d,t,w}

in particular a word that is not of the form C{a,u,o}C with a final
b/d/t/w can never be of the same family as dad,dab,gut,low,cat.

* ear   second a  third r ∉{b,d,t,w}
* cop   second o  third p ∉{b,d,t,w}
* ego   second g is not a vowel
* mom   second o  third m ∉{b,d,t,w}
* ate   second t is not a vowel

so the five negative exemplars are all correctly excluded.

On the five test items

* leg  second e ∉{a,u,o}
* dam  second a  third m ∉{b,d,t,w}
* rat  second a  third t ∈{b,d,t,w}
* car  second a  third r ∉{b,d,t,w}
* bin  second i ∉{a,u,o}

rat is the only item of the five that is of the form C{a,u,o}C with a
final b/d/t/w, i.e. the only item that is of the same family as
dad,dab,gut,low,cat.  In particular leg is a textbook non-member of
the family, e.g. the middle vowel is e and the final consonant is not
b/d/t/w.  dam, car and bin are non-members for the same reason.

